approaches.what:
A 'crypto' profile in config.json, deep-merged over the base, with:
- its own state dir (state/crypto) and a UTC-daily calendar with 365 periods/yr;
- fractional units and fee_bps;
- BTC-USD as benchmark and regime;
- a v1 universe of BTC and ETH, with time-series signals only (tsmom, trend, breakout);
- go to cash below SMA200 with a 2% band, vol target, 3x ATR trailing stop;
- decide on the completed UTC bar, fill at the 01:00 UTC 1-hour open.
The time machine and quant-critic run before any paper trading.

design:
ARCHITECTURE. One engine, two books. load_config(book) deep-merges config.json["books"]["crypto"] over the base. journal.use_book("crypto") points journal.STATE at state/crypto/, so portfolio, shadow, pending, overrides, predictions and trials.jsonl never mix with the stock book; a shared trials file would corrupt both DSR counts. CLI: --book crypto on every command. Stocks get an explicit "market" block holding today's constants, so the defaults reproduce current behaviour exactly (rule 5).

COMPONENTS (estimate: ~250 new or edited lines + ~200 test lines).
- aitrader/market.py (new) holds NyseCalendar and UtcDailyCalendar. NyseCalendar is today's _bar_is_final, _market_opened, official_opens and BDay cooldown, moved verbatim. The interface:
  - periods_per_year;
  - bar_is_final(bar, now): now >= bar + 24h + 5 min;
  - exec_time(decision_bar): bar + 1 day + exec_hour_utc;
  - fill_prices(names, exec_ts): open of the 1-hour bar starting at exec_ts, falling back to the 1-minute bar, then the daily open;
  - cooldown_until: counts bars, not business days.
- periods_per_year is threaded through signals.py:13, strategy.py:148, metrics.py:10, backtest.py:170-171 and broker.py:38. Using 252 understates crypto vol 1.2035x (measured on BTC), so positions come out ~20% too big.
- PaperBroker gains qty_step (stocks keep 1, today's floor) and fee_bps (stocks keep 0). Today a 10% target of $100k buys 0 BTC.
- strategy: per-symbol caps, group lists and the 10-name minimum come from config. VIX is skipped when market.vix=false; otherwise every live weekend goes defensive(no-vix).
- cycle: calendar calls replace the NY constants. Flags turn off three things: the earnings blackout (a Nasdaq failure sets "*", which blocks every non-ETF name), the overlays and corporate actions. The -0.06 intraday alert threshold moves to config.
- data: history "max" goes through period1/period2 and asserts meta.dataGranularity == "1d". range=max silently returns monthly bars.
- backtest: fee_bps, exec_delay_bps, and a variant list read from the profile.
- news_live stays untouched, and crypto never enters the stock universe.

DATA AND UNIVERSE. v1 uses Yahoo BTC-USD (daily from 2014-09-17) and ETH-USD (from 2017-11-09), the feed data.py already reads. The bars are UTC, include weekends, have no gaps, and adjclose equals close.

The two-coin list is chosen after the fact. Value-weighted survivorship bias is small (0.93%/yr vs 62.19%/yr equal-weighted, Liebi & Stöckl, secondary source), and the report must say so.

Live guard: if the Yahoo decision close differs from the Coinbase candle (no key needed) by more than 1%, skip the decision and alert. Yahoo's 2026-11-08 close sat ~20 bp below Coinbase and Kraken.

v2, only after v1 passes: a point-in-time top-N by trailing 30-day quote volume from the data.binance.vision archive, which keeps delisted pairs. Split a symbol's identity on data gaps; LUNAUSDT is two different coins.

SIGNALS. Time-series signals only; cross-sectional z-scores mean nothing across two names. tsmom 365/30, trend 50/200 and breakout 55, with priors 0.35/0.35/0.30 and the rest at 0. Lookbacks are translated once from the stock config (252 to 365, 21 to 30), not tuned. Learning is switched off explicitly; with fewer than 10 names, learn.py:21 would leave it silently inert.

RISK RULES (crypto profile, base values for the sweep).
- Regime: BTC close above SMA200 with the 2% band, risk_off_gross_mult 0 (cash). In-sample results (8 variants, no DSR, risk/out/a4_regime.txt):
  - BTC maxDD -67% vs -83% buy-and-hold; since 2022, -31% vs -67%;
  - ETH since 2018-06: -61% vs -86%;
  - 3-4 switches a year.
- target_vol_annual 0.30, against 2-year vol of 44.1% for BTC and 68.5% for ETH. The regime plus a 40% target gave BTC maxDD -46% over its full history; 0.30 should land near -35% (estimate).
- max_gross 1.0, no leverage. max_sector_pct 1.0, since the stock value of 0.30 would cap the whole book at 30%. In-book caps are BTC 1.0 and ETH 0.6, derived from risk-equivalent account caps (BTC 5%, ETH 3%) with crypto at 5% of the total.
- Stop: 3x ATR14 trailing, about 9.9% for BTC and 13.9% for ETH; 4-8% of random entries get stopped within 5 days. Not -3%: random entries touched -3% within 3 days 37.8% (BTC) and 51.4% (ETH) of the time, against 27.4% for the median stock. The -3% stop also added no edge: BTC 3-day mean -0.03% with it vs +0.04% without.
- Drawdown breaker scaled by vol (30/12): halve at -25%, flat at -50%. The stock thresholds of -10%/-20% would leave the book flat most of the time.
- Rebalance every 7 days, band 0.05, cooldown 14 bars, minimum trade $100. Fees run about 10x stock costs. The stock book turns over ~14-15x a year, which at 0.50% per side would cost ~7%/yr (arithmetic).
- Costs: fee 50 bp per side (an assumption between Alpaca's 25 bp and Kraken's 80 bp taker), 5 bp slippage, 10 bp exec delay; cash yield 0. VIX, earnings and overlays are off.

SCHEDULE. One idempotent scheduled task, every hour at :10; hourly is the scheduler's floor. Each run:
1. Checks the hash chains and fails closed.
2. Fills a pending decision whose exec time has passed, at the open of the 01:00 UTC 1-hour bar. A late run still uses that official price, as the stock book does with the 09:30 open.
3. Decides, if bar D is final (after 00:05 UTC on D+1) and has no decision yet, using data through that close.
4. Alerts only: a holding down 8% or more from the last daily close triggers a push, with no trade.

Stops are judged at the daily close, as the backtest assumes. Claude's reduce-only window is 00:10-01:00 UTC (02:10-03:00 Israel winter time), and overrides logged after 01:00 are ignored. Intraday stops wait for v2, tested on the Binance 1-hour archive.

DASHBOARD. A crypto section shows:
- equity of the crypto book vs its no-Claude shadow vs BTC buy-and-hold (and 50/50 BTC/ETH);
- positions in fractional units;
- a regime gauge (today BTC is +1.9% over its SMA200; risk-off below ~71,707);
- fees paid;
- the next decision and fill times in Israel time;
- overrides.
It also adds a total-paper line and crypto's share of it. Reports go to reports/crypto/. Benchmark labels come from cfg; SPY is hard-coded today in report.py, dashboard.py and index.html:496.

TESTING. All existing tests stay green, plus a golden test: the stock backtest on the cached panel gives identical results before and after the refactor. New tests:
- NoLookahead and truncation invariance on the UTC calendar;
- a 7-day CycleFlow: decide Saturday, fill Sunday 01:00, never decide on an unfinished bar, and a second run in the same hour does nothing new;
- fractional qty, fee accounting, cash never negative, and 365 bars = 1 year in metrics and mark;
- no VIX defensive mode on weekends;
- override cutoff = exec time;
- state isolation;
- regime fails closed without BTC.

Time machine: 2018-01-01 to today, all 7 weekly phases. Variants:
- fees 10/25/80 bp and exec delay 0/50 bp;
- no regime filter, and risk-off at 0.5;
- vol target 0.20/0.40;
- BTC-only, and +SOL (cap 0.4);
- ATR 2x/4x;
- stock breaker thresholds;
- monthly rebalance;
- regime-only.

Pass rule, written down before the run: the base beats BTC buy-and-hold on maxDD and Calmar in at least 5 of 7 phases, its Sharpe is no worse, and the sign holds at 80 bp and in both halves (2018-21 and 2022-26). DSR is reported, then the quant-critic reviews.

ROLLOUT.
1. Nimrod answers the owner questions.
2. Refactor commit; the stock book stays byte-identical.
3. Crypto profile commit.
4. Sweep saved to research/, a lesson recorded, and a quant-critic PASS.
5. Nimrod sees the result and approves paper trading.
6. Paper trading on the hourly task: no parameter changes for 3 months except reduce-only, with a monthly review against BTC.

Crypto news trading happens only if Nimrod chooses it, graded forward only, in a separate small book.
